+// kernel above). Here the only multiply is x 3, a single shift-add (ISCADD), and the "- 3 F_t" is moved out of
+// the byte lanes into the integer accumulators: with P_t = floor(x 3^t / 256) (the high byte of the 16-bit
+// lane x 3^t, x 3^5 = 58806 < 65536 so no lane overflow)
+//     sum_t digit_t * a_t = sum_t (P_{t+1} - 3 P_t) a_t = A - 3 B,   A = sum_t P_{t+1} a_t,  B = sum_t P_t a_t
+// A and B are exact int32 dp4a sums (P_t < 243: unsigned x signed dp4a), so sumi = A - 3 B is the same integer
+// as the digit walk and the fp32 result is bit-identical. 10 shift-adds + 7 PRMT + 9 dp4a per 4 packed bytes.
+// x * 3 as an explicit shift-add. nvcc folds `(x << 1) + x` and `x * 3` into mul.lo, which ptxas lowers to
